From: HarmonyOS Python Porting <porting@harmonyos.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Mar 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Modules/posixmodule.c: Add __OHOS__ cpu_count
 implementation

HarmonyOS supports sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN) via musl libc for
CPU count detection. Add an explicit __OHOS__ fallback branch in
os_cpu_count_impl() so that os.cpu_count() works correctly on
HarmonyOS even if the configure script does not properly detect
HAVE_SYSCONF or _SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN.

This patch has no corresponding 3.9 reference patch; it is newly
created for the 3.12 port.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [HarmonyOS specific]
---
 Modules/posixmodule.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Modules/posixmodule.c b/Modules/posixmodule.c
--- a/Modules/posixmodule.c
+++ b/Modules/posixmodule.c
@@ -14466,6 +14466,8 @@ os_cpu_count_impl(PyObject *module)
     mib[1] = HW_NCPU;
     if (sysctl(mib, 2, &ncpu, &len, NULL, 0) != 0)
         ncpu = 0;
+#elif defined(__OHOS__)
+    ncpu = sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN);
 #endif
     if (ncpu >= 1)
         return PyLong_FromLong(ncpu);
